commit 942ec38235105fe3ad58769dd82e029cd9139b2f
Author: Martin Oberzalek <martin.oberzalek@anton-paar.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 24 17:12:24 2026 +0200

    Log debug messages like the lotr_analyzer reference
    
    Add ToolLog::Session to libcommon. It installs an AsyncOut frontend as
    Tools::x_debug, optionally subscribes a timestamped file backend and a
    console backend, and owns the logger thread. Unlike the reference, which
    detaches its threads in main() and polls a quit flag, the session joins
    in its destructor, so a tool keeps one object alive and gets a
    guaranteed final drain.
    
    The three monitor tools call it as the first statement of main() and
    emit CPPDEBUG messages. The log file is requested with --log-file <path>;
    --debug adds the console backend. Both are opt-in, so
    list_monitor_resolutions.exe still prints its machine-readable list
    unchanged.
    
    Building this needed cpputils/io, which upstream keeps out of
    libcpputilsshared.a, so it is built here as cpputils/io/libcpputilsio.a.
    It requires -liconv: read_file.cc implements ReadFile::convert with
    iconv and DetectLocale calls it, and the link fails with "undefined
    reference to iconv_open" without it.
    
    New test subject src_test_rfa/test_debuglog covers the argv parsing, the
    line shape, append instead of truncate, and a frontend with no backend
    writing nothing. 68 testcases, all green.
    
    Also corrects the debug-logging skill: the timestamp does carry
    milliseconds, because %S prints the fractional part when the time point
    is finer than seconds. Its Makefile.am snippet was missing -liconv.

