    * rfa/RfaFormat.h - the container model from the 814-archive sweep: CHUNK_SIZE,
      BLOCK_HEADER_SIZE, CHUNK_DESCRIPTOR_SIZE, PayloadVariant, Chunk, Entry and
      chunk_count_for(). Header-only and I/O-free, so the arithmetic is testable in
      isolation from any file handling.
    * rfa/LzoCodec.h/.cc - miniLZO wrapper. An instance owns the compressor work
      buffer, so one per thread; decompress() is static and stateless, which means
      concurrent decompression needs no locking. compress() lets callers fall back to
      storing a chunk verbatim, because a chunk's compressedSize may legitimately
      exceed its uncompressedSize.
    * rfa/RfaArchive.h/.cc - reader for BOTH payload variants. Validates every
      invariant from the format model and collects complaints in problems() rather
      than failing hard. Parsing reads the table and the chunk descriptor tables but
      never a payload, so a 741 MB archive opens cheaply. PayloadReader holds its own
      file handle, which is what makes per-entry parallel extraction safe by
      construction rather than by convention.
    * src_test_rfa/test_rfa_format.{h,cc} - the model arithmetic, including the real
      fixture numbers rather than only round figures.
    * src_test_rfa/test_rfa_archive.{h,cc} - the reader against the fixtures.
    * src_test_rfa/test_lzo.{h,cc} - added LzoCodec wrapper cases.
    
    Coverage: all 259 entries across the four fixtures decompress to exactly their
    declared size, including 92 multi-chunk entries up to 22 chunks / 699,192 bytes,
    and the raw headerless variant. Corrupt input is rejected without crashing:
    truncated, garbage, empty, and payload-corrupted archives.
    
    Two gaps are recorded rather than papered over:
    * no fixture contains an Empty entry, so that variant is still untested; the
      writer will synthesise one.
    * the reader is self-consistent but NOT yet verified against the oracle - Phase 3
      compares against bin/rfaUnpack.orig.exe. The exception is
      archive_conquest_con_matches_phase0_ground_truth, which pins a real 373-byte
      file against bytes the original tool wrote to disk in Phase 0.
    
    RfaWriter, -u update and the multithreaded worker pool remain for part 2.

commit 0a4855e2e4b816dd00164becada8633bb432913d
